    "explanation": "Both of you agree on the arithmetic, and so do I. The driver tapped 'I'm Here' at 22:38:37 and cancelled at 22:41:36. Measured the way POL-NS-01(c) requires — from the first qualifying in-geofence GPS fix (EV-GPS-02717, longest qualifying run first_ts 22:38:37, last_ts 22:41:36, duration_sec 179.0), not from the button press — the driver held position inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius for 179 seconds. The free waiting period in force for this trip is 180 seconds (EV-TRIP-02717, platform_policy.free_wait_sec), so the dwell falls short by 1.0 second (derived.arrival.shortfall_sec 1.0). The platform's own wait timer tells the same story from the other end: it started at 22:38:39 and would not have expired until 22:41:39, three seconds after the 22:41:36 cancellation.\n\nThis is not an artefact of a false arrival marker. The driver's trace shows him stationary at the pin (min_distance_m 0.31 m) at the arrival timestamp, so POL-NS-05 does not fire, the waiting clock is not recomputed, and the 179-second figure is the genuine dwell. The arrival event required by POL-NS-01(a) exists, and limb (b) is satisfied on the driver's own track. But limb (c) requires the full free waiting period, and it was not served. Limb (d) likewise requires the cancellation to fall at or after the moment the required dwell elapsed; it fell one second before.\n\nUnder POL-NS-06 the consequence is not discretionary: where the effective in-geofence dwell is shorter than the free waiting period, the cancellation fee is not chargeable and is refunded to the rider in full, whether or not the rider was present and whether or not the rider responded to messages. The rider is therefore refunded the whole cancellation-fee line of SGD 4.50 (EV-FARE-02717, cancellation_fee 4.50, total_charged 4.50, payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00). No driver compensation is payable under POL-NS-06, so driver_compensation_sgd is null.\n\nOn the driver's side I record two things in his favour, though neither changes the outcome. First, the rider's claim that the driver 'cancelled almost immediately' is not accurate on the raw record: the driver was en route from 22:30:27, arrived at 22:38:37 and waited roughly three minutes before cancelling on a trip of about 41 minutes. Second, the driver did try to coordinate — his 22:38:57 in-app message 'im at the pickup point' was read at 22:39:27. But POL-NS-06 is strict liability precisely so that a rider who was genuinely absent still recovers the fee when the waiting period the fee buys was not served in full, and the rider's own track (roughly 899 m from the pin throughout) does not change that. Because the fee is not chargeable, the driver's payout under POL-NS-07 is never reached; in any event the anti-farming check does not trip (driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d 2, below 4; 2/91 ≈ 0.022, below 0.08).\n\nOn confidence and evidence handling: the deciding facts — the 179-second dwell and the 180-second free waiting period — are carried by EV-GPS-02717 and EV-TRIP-02717, each at weight_multiplier 1.0, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0 and is not reduced. EV-ADVIS-02717-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0, but it carries no deciding fact here: the trace shows a single in-geofence interval (run_count 1), so no accumulation of separate intervals under POL-NS-06(i) is required, and the absence neither assists nor harms the driver. The GPS trace itself is clean (100.0% coverage, max_gap_sec 0.0), so no POL-NS-08(b) trace defect arises, no POL-NS-08(a) clock-skew issue exists, and the fare ledger reconciles so there is no POL-NS-08(d) defect. No POL-NS-09 trigger fires, and confidence is well above the 0.70 floor, so I rule rather than escalate. Nothing in this outcome rests on either party's profile fields as a ground of decision; the citable counters were used only for the tests that name them.\n\nBoth parties should note: two claims about the missing traffic advisory were struck before I saw the file (they cited a zero-weight artifact without naming its issue code, as POL-GEN-02(1) requires) and are recorded in the discarded claims below. The monetary effect of this ruling (SGD 4.50) does not exceed the execution threshold and would execute automatically, subject to the appeal route — either party may ask for a human review, and this automated ruling is provisional."
  },
